      "tituloOriginal": "Southwest of Southwestern Mexico (EP99)",
      "descripcion": "Showers and thunderstorms associated with a broad area of low pressure located about 350 miles south of Manzanillo, Mexico have changed little in organization since earlier today. However, environmental conditions remain conducive for development, and an increase in the organization of the system could result in it becoming a tropical depression or storm within the next day or so. The system is expected to move eastward off the coast of southern Mexico on Monday, but could begin moving toward the coast by late Tuesday. Interests along the southwestern and west-central coast of Mexico should monitor the progress of this system. For more information, including gale warnings, see the High Seas Forecast issued by the National Weather Service.",
